              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A method can change an aggregate after it reached a terminal state."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A public method has no guard that stops it once a state field holds a declared terminal value, so it can still change an aggregate that is meant to be finished. A cancelled order that can still be shipped, or a closed account that still takes deposits, is a broken business rule."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Guard the method with an early return or throw on the state field so it cannot run from the terminal value. If changing a finished aggregate is intended, as for a remove method, list the method in allowAfterTerminal in domain.config.ts. Accept the finding into the baseline only while it is a known defect you mean to fix.",
                "markdown": "Guard the method with an early return or throw on the state field so it cannot run from the terminal value. If changing a finished aggregate is intended, as for a remove method, list the method in allowAfterTerminal in domain.config.ts. Accept the finding into the baseline only while it is a known defect you mean to fix.\\n\\n[Rule reference](https://github.com/mannkostir/domain-integrity#terminal-state-leak)"
