              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A method can run from states its declared transition does not allow, or sets the state field without a declared transition."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A method can run from states that its entry in transitions does not list, or it sets the state field while transitions has no entry for it. The code then allows more than the declared lifecycle, so the declaration no longer describes what the aggregate does."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Add a guard that excludes the extra states, or, if the code is right, add those states to the method's entry in transitions in domain.config.ts, or add an entry for a method that has none. Accept the finding into the baseline only while it is a known defect you mean to fix.",
                "markdown": "Add a guard that excludes the extra states, or, if the code is right, add those states to the method's entry in transitions in domain.config.ts, or add an entry for a method that has none. Accept the finding into the baseline only while it is a known defect you mean to fix.\\n\\n[Rule reference](https://github.com/mannkostir/domain-integrity#transition-drift)"
